;;; One candidate, refuted in TWO firings — M1e2 **W2**, the forced-positive
;;; cascade refuting a consistent program, at **default flags**. Register row
;;; `W2/forced-2` (`corpus/wrong_answers.toml`).
;;;
;;; ── The program ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; One object. `(q one)` taints it, a taint is a contradiction, so `(q one)`
;;; dies — in two firings, one past what the pre-branch lookahead simulates.
;;; `:no-hypothesis (bad)` keeps the rung off the taint itself.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Without any hypothesis the program is consistent, and the one hypothesis
;;; there is dies. Root is the solution (Q-M1e.6, clause 3): **`Solution`,
;;; k = 1, a model with no `q` fact.**
;;;
;;; ── What the engine says ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;;   solutions (k)   0
;;;   verdict         No solution — the constraints are contradictory
;;;   unsat core (0 facts)
;;;   exhausted        true
;;;   enterings        0
;;;
;;; The lookahead cannot see a two-firing death, so `alive = {(q one)}`, a
;;; singleton, and `promote_forced_positives` writes `(q one)` into **root**
;;; with a premise-less `<forced-positive>` provenance. Root is then
;;; contradictory, `root_dead` refutes the run, and the refutation is
;;; certified with no fact behind it. No commitment was ever entered.
;;;
;;; ── Twins ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `forced-2-off.ein` is this file plus `(config :enable-forced-positive
;;; false)`: the cascade off, it still answers `Contradiction` — now through
;;; W1 at layer 0, with a 1-fact core. Fixing W2 alone falls through into W1,
;;; which is why P1e2.2 orders S1e2.2.1 first. `forced-1.ein` is the
;;; one-firing twin, right at default flags and wrong the same way under `-L`.
;;;
;;; Banked from M1e2's probes at S1e2.1.1.
(relation thing T)
(relation q T)
(relation bad T)
(thing one)
(rule taint () :match (q ?x)   :assert (bad ?x) :priority 200)
(rule kill  () :match (bad ?x) :assert (false)  :priority 300)
(solve :no-hypothesis (bad))
(query :goal (thing ?x))
